{"body":{"text":["What a session knows is in the field; memory is off, \"OpenLight had to set this boundary early\" (2/6). A session is kept whole in his words, every utterance as said, its answers by their essence, read against the transcripts by blank agents before it is trusted (11/105, 13/129). What matters in it is lifted into the elevation, below."]},"id":"1M89K3DW7D3N000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field is written today by the author's tools in `author/`, through the engine: `session.ts` keeps a session, `append.ts` adds an utterance, `thread.ts` raises and moves a thread, and `rewrite.ts` rewrites briefs; `author/README.md` says how. They are to go once the command line can commit, as the way from here orders, the author's direction being away from such rigid scripts toward clear types and structure and practices held as skills, so an agent knows how to work and does the work with the engine directly (15/31). Meanwhile `rewrite.ts` can change words inside a paragraph it keeps, which invites the patching Knowledge's own rule forbids, and the twenty-third session patched so: \"patching, I think, is forbidden under the rules\" (23/144). Whether the tools go now or wait for commits written in the field, \"I don't know if we should remove them yet, or if we're waiting for the better commit expressions to come in place\" (23/146), the author leaves as a note (23/148). *Open.* One practice holds meanwhile: when Knowledge is regenerated, it keeps its id, and every sentence whose text is unchanged keeps its holon."]},"id":"1M89K3DW7D3N001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}